dniv_unique_pfams
```


how to put summary data from two taxa together

make the summary opject for two or more taxa, omitting the top and slice functions. change the summarize section to have object  num_pfams_dniv for example 

```{r}
#putting PFAMs side by side

num_empty_rows_hetero <- 2 
empty_rows <- tibble(
  PFAMs = rep(NA_character_, num_empty_rows_hetero),
  num_fam = rep(NA_real_, num_empty_rows_hetero)
)

filtered_heterobasidion2 <- bind_rows(filtered_heterobasidion, empty_rows)

#The above code created a table two empty columns with the headers PFAMs and num_fam respectively, both with two empty rows. the rep function placed the character NA in the PFAM column because the PFAM column uses strings. It placed NA in the num_fam column with NA_real_ because this column deals with numbers. 

#The bind_rows function appends the empty_rows table to the bottom of the filtered_heterobasidion table. 

#trying to rearrange the rows of the filtered_heterobasidion 2

filtered_heterobasidion2 <- tibble(
  PFAMs= c("Chromo,RVP_2,RVT_1,Retrotrans_gag,rve,zf-CCHC", "Chromo,Peptidase_A2E,RVT_1,rve", "rve", "gag-asp_proteas", "DUF5314,RVT_2,gag_pre-integrs,rve,zf-CCHC", "p450", "MFS_1", "RVT_2,Retrotran_gag_2,gag_pre-integrs,rve", "Pkinase", "RVT_2,Retrotran_gag_2,gag_pre-integrs,rve,zf-CCHC", "Asp_protease_2", "Retrotran_gag_2,gag_pre-integrs,rve", "WD40", "RVT_2,gag_pre-integrs,rve", "adh_short", "Sugar_tr", "RVP_2", "GMC_oxred_C,GMC_oxred_N", "RRM_1", "Chromo"),
  num_fam=c("121","15","75","32","NA","115","100","9","107","NA","4","27","53","4","25","36","23", "27", "39", "7")
)

#Basically what happened here is I put all the data in manually based on the information in the previous iteration of the filtered_heterobasidion2 table created above.

